  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-03-12T18:24:27.421Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Community player moderators would be a nice additions to combat the amount of hacked clients, crash avatars, and general community based issues with VRChat. \nI have over 7500 hours of VRChat playtime and I have never seen a single community mod. I believe that adding a application based, interview, playtime history, closely monitored position on the VRChat team of a \"Community Player Moderator\" would be beneficial to the games health. The unfortunate truth about VRChat is that the game has a dark side to it. (Players who install clients that allow them to ignore safety settings or destroy a players experience with crashing or removing floors from worlds, etc.) \nIn most large social games, there are player moderators who can combat these types of players by issuing bans or kicks from worlds. I'm not talking about a single player for 1 world, but a player/community mod who has the permissions to ban players in any world. I'm aware this topic was brought up last year, but I would like to bring more attention to the subject as I believe it would be healthy for the game. Thanks!",
